WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Hey, it is Will. Here is how you set up the Intelligent Growth Connector.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
This also works in ChatGPT settings, but for Claude, jump into Customize.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Scroll down to Connectors.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Click Add in the top right, then click Add custom connector.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Add the name, Intelligent Growth Connector, then grab the URL.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Use mcp.intelligentgrowth.app/mcp, then click Add and Connect.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The sign-in page opens. Enter your email and connect.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:10.000
That takes a moment. Open Claude again once it is connected.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Now it is connected. Jump back into the Connector settings.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
I personally turn on Always allow for the tools, so Claude can use them when needed.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Now copy the starter prompt from the setup guide and paste it into a new chat.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:51.000
You can use this prompt or another product marketing job you want to run.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:04.000
I am using Granola as the example company.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:27.000
It works better when we include the company URL, so I will add granola.ai and let it run.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Claude goes through the tools. If you did not select Always allow, approve each tool as it runs.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Now it is running the positioning diagnosis.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Here is the diagnosis, including the biggest positioning risk and the missing evidence.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:14.000
It has given us a useful first analysis. That diagnosis is available on the free plan.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:36.000
For more, I can ask it to improve the positioning or create a full positioning, messaging and go-to-market plan.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.869
It will ask a series of questions so you can get started. That is how you set it up.
